fullDescription:
Dice Thrower is a game-agnostic dice companion for tabletop and role-playing games.

Create characters with a name, optional image, free-form game tag and level. Define reusable variables such as Strength, Intelligence or any modifier your game needs, then reference them directly inside roll formulas. Level up once and every parameterized roll updates automatically.

Build your own quick-roll dashboard with groups and ungrouped actions. The compact editor keeps large collections manageable with direct access plus explicit up/down controls and drag-and-drop ordering. The roll builder keeps named Roll Parts, such as attack and damage, independent. Each part has one validated text formula linked to a visual Formula Composer, including parentheses, variables and scalar multiplication.

Main features:
• configurable characters, levels and custom modifiers;
• compact grouped and ungrouped quick-roll dashboards with fast reordering;
• independent named Roll Parts with validated editable formulas and a synchronized visual composer;
• d2, d3, d4, d6, d8, d10, d12, d20 and d100;
• parameterized expressions and automatic positive or negative level scaling;
• configurable first-roll and reroll triggers using tap, upward swipe, phone motion, or the always-available footer dice icon;
• full-screen animated 3D dice table with ergonomic controls, quick Roll edit and character level adjustments in statistics, and Android Back navigation;
• ten premium built-in table artworks with visual previews, or your own custom table photo, including portrait images cropped without distortion;
• portable table photos preserved through local backup and optional Google Drive sync;
• dice that settle progressively on the engine-selected result face, plus per-die appearance, grouped statistics and local roll history;
• versioned local backup and restore through Android's document picker;
• optional Google Drive sync across devices, with standalone always available;
• light and dark themes;
• multilingual interface.

Dice Thrower is offline-first. No account is required: standalone mode keeps character data, settings and roll history on the device. Google connection is optional and can be disconnected without deleting the local copy. The app contains no advertising, analytics or tracking. Backup files are created only when you explicitly choose a destination.
